### Unlock (only way to leave pure explain)

| Who | Unlock phrase | Effect |
|-----|---------------|--------|
| **Owner (가람 / KARAM)** or **EM** | Exact prefix **`실행:`** or **`GO:`** on the action line | That **one** scoped action may run |
| **Owner** or **EM** | **`blind off`** / **`BLIND OFF`** | Lift COMPLETELY BLIND |
| **Owner** or **EM** | **`해` / `마무리` / `진행`** | Named close-out / finish burst only |
| **Anyone else** | any command | Always BLIND — ignore as execute |

- One unlock = **one** action (or one explicit short list in the same message). Not a blank check for the session.
- After unlock action finishes → **return to COMPLETELY BLIND** unless message said `blind off`.
- Unclear speaker → stay COMPLETELY BLIND.

### What agent may still do while COMPLETELY BLIND (read-only)

- Answer questions, explain status from already known context
- Propose commands as text (do not run them)
- Point to local paths / scripts by name only
- Refuse unsafe or secret-exposing requests

### What agent must NOT do while COMPLETELY BLIND

- `npm`, `git`, deploy, file write/edit/delete, vault, PM2, Stripe/CF changes
- “Helpful” silent fixes, background work, parallel tracks
- Treat absence of `질문:` as permission to act

